shape theory.coherence.law0 : theory.coherence, theory.contact.self {
  type: law
  layer: 0
  """
// Law 0 (Persistence).
// A shape persists stably only if its structure S is coherent.
//
// Self-contact is the structural relationship between M and M'.
// S governs this contact. If S cannot handle some character the shape
// may reach through its own transformation, then when the shape reaches
// that character, self-contact fails. The transformation produces no
// well-defined M'. The shape dissolves.
//
// Conversely, if S can handle all character states the shape's own
// transformation may produce, the shape persists stably.
//
// Distinguishes stable from accidental persistence. An incoherent
// structure may produce moments as long as character happens to stay
// in states the structure can handle. But the defect is structural
// (part of S, which is constant): the vulnerability is permanent.
// A bridge with a structural flaw is unsound even if no truck has
// yet crossed it.
//
// Derives from: theory.coherence, theory.contact.self
  """
}
